From 395b78dd8eeb0153fbaa6a3884d30c1d650031dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:34:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/36] Visual references: the object, the resolver and the
 table behind them

A character reference accumulates. On day one it is a name, three words and
a photograph; on day thirty it is twenty-five curated images, a hero seed, a
preset that works and a trained LoRA. Every field is optional and the
resolver uses whatever is there, which is what makes the object useful with
no image backend installed at all.

The resolver is pure on purpose: no clock, no dice, no Dexie. The caller
rolls the explore seed, so two calls with the same arguments give the same
result and a recipe diff means something. It also explains itself, step by
step, because a writer who cannot see what was sent cannot learn the tool.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
